  <rules>
    <rule id="bfca-95d3-0f2c-a8d6" name="Ancestral Grudge" hidden="false">
      <description>Dwarfs Hate all Greenskins: every kind of Orc, Goblin and Snotling, including Night Goblins, Black Orcs, Hobgoblins and Gnoblars.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d381-d4a7-3819-afb8" name="Resolute" hidden="false">
      <description>Dwarfs (but not Gyrocopters) flee and pursue 2D6-1&quot; instead of the normal 2D6&quot;.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="14cd-ffc1-3bfb-6e49" name="Relentless" hidden="false">
      <description>Dwarf units may march even if there are enemy units close enough to normally prevent marching.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3671-5549-dc55-e6ed" name="Rules of the Runes" hidden="false">
      <description>--- PLEASE CHECK THIS MANUALLY. BATTLESCRIBE CANNOT ENFORCE ALL OF THESE ---

A character may have at most one runic item of each type (one runic weapon, one runic armour, one runic talisman, and so on). A runic item follows all the normal rules for magic items. A character with a runic melee weapon may still carry a crossbow, handgun or pistol, but a pistol cannot be used alongside a runic melee weapon for +1 Attack.

1) Rule of Three: no item may carry more than three runes.
2) Rule of Form: weapon runes only on weapons, armour runes only on armour, standard runes only on standards, engineering runes only on war machines, talismanic runes only on talismans.
3) Rule of Pride: no two items in the army may carry the same combination of runes, and this includes single runes (two characters may not both have armour with just a Rune of Resistance, for example). The Rune of Stone is an exception.
4) Jealous Runes: each master rune may be used only once per army, and no item may carry more than one master rune.
5) Other runes may be combined freely and used in multiples, with cumulative effects, unless the rune says otherwise.

Weapon runes: none of the bonuses or penalties of the original weapon apply to a runic weapon, which simply counts as a magic weapon. The one exception is the Master Rune of Kragg the Grim.

Runic standards: master runes may only be placed on the Battle Standard.</description>
    </rule>
  </rules>
  <sharedSelectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry id="7895-d575-6d13-ddc0" name="Anvil of Doom" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <constraints>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="b852-f27f-843d-5395" type="max"/>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="roster" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="true" id="3116-216c-f717-98c5" type="max"/>
      </constraints>
      <profiles>
        <profile id="ad91-9ab0-eb63-fe32" name="Anvil Guard (2)" hidden="false" typeId="0a0f-00cd-0261-c0ea" typeName="Model">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="M" typeId="da3c-fb2b-4c5f-a22b">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="WS" typeId="d46f-1ae5-387f-4ac3">5</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="BS" typeId="22c7-799b-e07c-f32c">3</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="S" typeId="0c58-1252-962d-8fcc">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="T" typeId="16d7-9f22-06d8-8427">4</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="W" typeId="f9d0-a5b0-7e0b-a404">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="I" typeId="b418-0e30-644f-1435">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="A" typeId="fa03-f9a3-8117-98dd">1</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="bbad-d421-400b-87c1">9</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule id="d0c2-8e8c-5854-b38d" name="Anvil of Doom" hidden="false">
          <description>0-1 per army. Taken by a Runelord, who then also uses up a Hero choice. The Anvil is a war machine that cannot be moved or attacked in any way. It comes with two Anvil Guards (hand weapon, gromril armour and shield).

The Runelord and both Guards stay on the platform all battle. They are Unbreakable, may not declare charges and never pursue. The Anvil and crew have Unit Strength 5, and no other character may join them. Enemies charging the Anvil are placed in base contact with the platform; the Runelord and Guards place themselves between the enemy and the Anvil, and fight as a unit with a 60mm frontage.

Shooting at the Anvil: randomise hits evenly between the remaining Dwarfs, who have a 4+ ward save against all missiles, including magic missiles.

Victory Points: the Runelord as normal; if the Runelord and both Guards are killed, the Anvil&apos;s Victory Points are scored too.

Dispel dice: while the Runelord lives the Anvil adds one dice to the Dwarf Dispel pool.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="59aa-38d4-b6af-682c" name="Striking Runes" hidden="false">
          <description>In his own Shooting phase the Runelord may strike one rune per turn, but not if he or the Guards are in close combat. Choose to strike it normally (succeeds on a 2+) or with Ancient Power (succeeds on a 4+). If the roll fails, roll on the Failed Rune table:

1: Disaster! The Anvil splits in two. Remove the Anvil, the Runelord and the Anvil Guards as casualties.
2-3: The Runelord draws more power than he can control. No effect, and the Anvil may not be used next turn.
4-6: The rune is struck incorrectly. No effect this turn.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="ec29-cdf2-8281-d575" name="Rune of Hearth &amp; Hold" hidden="false">
          <description>Every friendly Dwarf unit may re-roll failed Fear and Terror tests until the start of the owning player&apos;s next Shooting phase (no re-roll of a re-roll).

Ancient Power: all friendly Dwarf units may instead re-roll failed Panic and Break tests and are immune to fear and terror for that time.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="d4af-56e7-3a87-fad0" name="Rune of Oath &amp; Honour" hidden="false">
          <description>One friendly Dwarf unit (not a Gyrocopter) may make a normal move (which may be a march or a charge) in the Shooting phase. It may not shoot that phase, and a unit that rallied this turn may not make the move.

Ancient Power: D3 friendly Dwarf units are affected.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="78c1-33dd-7676-b733" name="Rune of Wrath &amp; Ruin" hidden="false">
          <description>Nominate an unengaged enemy unit anywhere on the table (not an independent character unless it, or its mount, is a large target). It takes D6 magical Strength 4 hits, distributed as shooting. A unit that can fly cannot fly in its next Movement phase; a non-flyer halves its Movement until the end of its own following turn. If forced to flee in that time it flees at half speed (roll as normal, halve, round up).

Ancient Power: D3 enemy units are affected, each taking 2D6 magical Strength 4 hits.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink id="c629-6a08-b8c1-1800" name="Unbreakable" hidden="false" targetId="f6c9-ac44-1d7c-ed6e" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="eaa7-6800-e651-8bea" value="175.0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="4ba1-9912-d887-206c" name="Rangers" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="increment" field="eaa7-6800-e651-8bea" value="1.0">
          <repeats>
            <repeat field="selections" scope="parent" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" childId="model" repeats="1" roundUp="false"/>
          </repeats>
        </modifier>
        <modifier type="increment" field="fb7d-6169-e093-aabc" value="1.0">
          <conditions>
            <condition field="selections" scope="roster" value="1.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="true" childId="f849-62c5-26a1-4c44" type="atLeast"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <constraints>
