        <entryLink id="a4b4-46ab-42a6-ad6e" name="Runic Talismans" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="d356-0bbb-0239-a9e7" type="selectionEntryGroup">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition field="selections" scope="parent" value="0.0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" childId="b430-9309-4c29-d0cf" type="instanceOf"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
        </entryLink>
      </entryLinks>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="722f-36f1-adcd-e612" name="Dwarf Handgun" hidden="false">
      <description>Maximum range 24&quot;, Strength 4. Armour piercing; move-or-fire. Superior design: a Dwarf handgun has a +1 to hit modifier.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1227-43bb-2b96-c63e" name="Gromril Armour" hidden="false">
      <description>Gromril armour gives a 4+ armour save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2c93-feb2-a188-9f46" name="Oath Stone" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the game a character with an Oath stone nominates a unit of Warriors (but not Rangers), Longbeards, Ironbreakers or Hammerers as his Stonebearers. He must deploy with that unit and may not leave it. The stone gives the unit Magic Resistance (1). No other character may join a Stonebearer unit.

While the character lives, if the Stonebearer unit is charged he may &apos;set the stone&apos; as part of a Hold reaction. From then on:
1) The unit has no flanks or rear, even if the character is later killed: it keeps its rank bonus when charged in the flank or rear, and enemies get no flank or rear combat resolution bonus against it.
2) The unit may not move unless forced to flee, and may not choose to flee as a charge reaction. The character may not be moved within the unit.
3) The character must always issue and accept challenges.
4) If the unit flees the Oath stone is lost, and the Victory Points for the character are lost whether or not he survives.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1cb2-d622-cad7-ac39" name="Royal Blood" hidden="false">
      <description>Dwarf Lords (but not Thanes) are of Royal Blood. Used with the Hammerers&apos; Bodyguard rule. An army containing a character with Royal Blood may have one more unit of Longbeards than it has units of Warriors.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a431-2cd4-cc10-850d" name="Rune Lore" hidden="false">
      <description>A Runesmith gives the Dwarf player an extra Dispel dice in the enemy Magic phase. A Runelord gives two extra Dispel dice.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9b1c-0927-da1a-78f0" name="Slayer" hidden="false">
      <description>When rolling to wound, a Slayer&apos;s Strength (including weapon modifiers) is increased to equal the Toughness of his opponent, up to a maximum of Strength 6. If the opponent&apos;s Toughness is lower than the Slayer&apos;s Strength he gets no bonus. Armour save modifiers use the modified Strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0039-b6fd-1f4a-0a8d" name="Slayer Axes" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of each combat a Slayer unit chooses to fight either with two axes (counting as an additional hand weapon) or with a single axe in both hands (counting as a great weapon), and keeps that choice until the combat ends. A Slayer with a rune axe fights with it alone, as a hand weapon, or as a great weapon if it bears the Master Rune of Kragg the Grim.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7f43-c61d-6a5a-5b22" name="Loner" hidden="false">
      <description>Daemon Slayers and Dragon Slayers may only fight alone or join a Slayers unit. They can never be the army&apos;s General.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5a6b-b805-0d7d-6978" name="Gunners&apos; Pride" hidden="false">
      <description>Dwarfs crewing a war machine (and Master Engineers or Engineers who have joined it as additional crew) are Stubborn as long as the machine has not been destroyed. They may never choose to flee as a charge reaction or pursue a fleeing enemy. Does not apply to the Gyrocopter.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5a5e-1e29-078f-03ba" name="Additional Crew" hidden="false">
      <description>Dwarf artillery follows the rulebook rules for loss of crew. A Master Engineer or Engineer with a war machine may act as crew, and suffers the consequences of any Misfire. In each Shooting phase he either acts as additional crew, uses his Artillery Master or Artillery Specialist rule, or fires his own weapons; declare which before the machine fires.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2d3c-3491-9e13-86e8" name="Artillery Specialist" hidden="false">
      <description>An Engineer in a war machine crew: with a Bolt Thrower you may use his BS when firing; with a Grudge Thrower or Cannon, if the machine Misfires you may re-roll the result on its Misfire chart.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="56b6-ef62-252c-fd21" name="Master Rune of Skalf Blackhammer" hidden="false">
      <description>Always wounds on 2+ whatever the target&apos;s Toughness. The Strength needed to wound on a 2+ is used for armour save modifiers (against Toughness 4 that is Strength 6, so -3).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="55a2-aa49-30f0-93b0" name="Master Rune of Smiting" hidden="false">
      <description>An enemy wounded by this weapon (after saves) takes D6 wounds instead of 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="69b4-aebe-2f50-15e4" name="Master Rune of Alaric the Mad" hidden="false">
      <description>No armour save is allowed against wounds from this weapon.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="326b-eb3d-921b-e7da" name="Master Rune of Breaking" hidden="false">
      <description>If the wielder hits an enemy armed with a magic weapon, that magic weapon is destroyed immediately.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bcdd-a7e0-8905-41f5" name="Master Rune of Flight" hidden="false">
      <description>May not be used by Slayer characters. Works as a thrown weapon with a 12&quot; range that may target any enemy model in the wielder&apos;s line of sight that is not in close combat. The target is automatically hit once as if in close combat (so the other runes on the weapon apply), then the hammer returns. May also be used in close combat as a hand weapon, where this rune only makes it magical.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8539-cbf8-0f7e-79f1" name="Master Rune of Swiftness" hidden="false">
      <description>The wielder always strikes first, even against chargers. If both sides strike first, the higher Initiative goes first; ties follow the rulebook&apos;s Who Strikes First rules.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5caa-e8e2-7246-d394" name="Master Rune of Kragg the Grim" hidden="false">
      <description>May only be placed on great weapons. The great weapon keeps its normal abilities (+2 Strength, strikes last, etc.), which weapon runes otherwise remove.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4a2d-1a44-4fa6-cdd1" name="Rune of Might" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. The wielder&apos;s Strength is doubled against enemies with Toughness 5 or more.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1eab-87e7-3ebe-163d" name="Rune of Snorri Spangelhelm" hidden="false">
      <description>+1 to hit with this weapon. Multiple runes are cumulative, but the roll needed to hit can never be better than 2+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b16a-d6bc-7981-268a" name="Rune of Fury" hidden="false">
      <description>The wielder adds +1 to his Attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4156-f992-9bfa-be3f" name="Rune of Cleaving" hidden="false">
      <description>The wielder adds +1 to his Strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7ee6-d32f-3bf4-1546" name="Grudge Rune" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. Before the game secretly note one enemy character or monster on your roster; the wielder may re-roll misses in close combat against that model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1d62-6104-496a-b21f" name="Rune of Striking" hidden="false">
      <description>The wielder adds +1 to his Weapon Skill.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="42a7-ff5f-b434-b5ce" name="Rune of Speed" hidden="false">
      <description>The wielder adds +1 to his Initiative.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7288-819b-e385-6517" name="Rune of Fire" hidden="false">
      <description>The weapon makes Flaming attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="754b-be4f-7184-bf0f" name="Master Rune of Steel" hidden="false">
      <description>Attacks against the bearer with a Strength greater than 5 are treated as Strength 5.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6c2f-7b0d-9f3e-4ea4" name="Master Rune of Adamant" hidden="false">
      <description>+1 to the character&apos;s Toughness.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bae3-f572-9aae-fedf" name="Master Rune of Gromril" hidden="false">
      <description>The armour gives a 1+ armour save that cannot be improved in any way.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1316-211b-aaeb-849b" name="Rune of Fortitude" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer gains +1 Wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8ecf-6b78-e0db-7da3" name="Rune of Shielding" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. 2+ ward save against shooting attacks and spells defined as magic missiles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fd08-525c-e9bc-a214" name="Rune of Resistance" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. The character may re-roll failed armour saves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9288-ed4d-c4ea-1f2a" name="Rune of Iron" hidden="false">
      <description>6+ ward save. Two Runes of Iron give a 5+ ward save; three may not be taken.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f9db-796c-f0d3-49cb" name="Rune of Preservation" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. Immune to Killing Blow and Poisoned Attacks: attacks on this model are resolved as if the attacker did not have them.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1080-5570-a285-6abc" name="Rune of Stone" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. +1 to the character&apos;s armour save. An exception to the Rule of Pride: any number of characters&apos; armour may bear a single Rune of Stone.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0c44-186a-baaa-035f" name="Master Rune of Kingship" hidden="false">
      <description>May only be engraved on the crown of a Dwarf Lord. The Lord and the unit he leads are Stubborn and immune to fear and terror.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8abc-5d9e-6479-822f" name="Master Rune of Balance" hidden="false">
      <description>Runesmiths and Runelords only. In each enemy Magic phase, remove one dice from the opponent&apos;s Power dice pool and add it to your Dispel dice pool.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d54a-88e5-fc2c-7b43" name="Master Rune of Spellbinding" hidden="false">
      <description>Runesmiths and Runelords only. +1 to all dispel attempts made by the owning player.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="454c-eca7-33c0-1493" name="Master Rune of Spite" hidden="false">
      <description>4+ ward save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="69f0-59e0-696b-86bb" name="Master Rune of Challenge" hidden="false">
      <description>One use only. Used in the enemy turn before charges are declared: nominate one enemy unit within 20&quot; that is able to charge and reach the rune bearer (or his unit). It must either charge him (and any unit he is with) or flee in the Compulsory Movement phase as if it had failed a Panic test. No effect on units immune to psychology.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="99ab-f9d0-bd73-27dd" name="Master Rune of Dismay" hidden="false">
      <description>One use only. Used in the enemy turn before charges are declared: every enemy unit on the table that is not immune to psychology takes a Leadership test, and if it fails may not declare a charge that turn. Units that move in the Compulsory Movement phase are not affected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6e7a-12f1-5525-cd72" name="Spelleater Rune" hidden="false">
      <description>Runesmiths and Runelords only. One use only. Works exactly like a Rune of Spellbreaking; in addition, on a 4+ the dispelled spell is lost to the caster for the rest of the game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f088-593f-04ee-dcff" name="Rune of Fate" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. One use only. 2+ ward save against the first wound suffered that is not saved by armour.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="54d9-d296-4513-b395" name="Rune of Spellbreaking" hidden="false">
      <description>Runesmiths and Runelords only. One use only. Automatically dispels one enemy spell with no roll needed. Does not work against spells cast with Irresistible Force.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d3cf-0c8c-25b0-86c3" name="Rune of Brotherhood" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. One use only. May not be used by a character with an Oath stone or Shieldbearers. The character may either deploy with a unit of Rangers using its Scout rule as if he had it himself, or join a unit of Miners using its Underground Advance rule and arrive with them.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="30c5-5656-770a-c819" name="Rune of Luck" hidden="false">
      <description>One use only. The bearer may re-roll any single to hit roll, to wound roll, armour save or ward save during the game.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d0a5-2ef3-1173-5445" name="Rune of Warding" hidden="false">
      <description>Each rune gives cumulative Magic Resistance (1) to the character and the unit he is with.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="de75-41ba-7645-dc0b" name="Rune of the Furnace" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer is immune to fire: he cannot be affected by attacks consisting purely of flaming attacks, such as Fire Balls, Skaven Warpfire Throwers or a High Elf Dragon&apos;s breath.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="82b0-c5f9-b95b-9ebb" name="Master Rune of Valaya" hidden="false">
      <description>+2 to all dispel attempts made by the owning player. Any remains-in-play spell affecting a target within 12&quot; of the standard is dispelled automatically at the start of either player&apos;s Magic phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="797a-ca5a-b266-a22e" name="Master Rune of Stromni Redbeard" hidden="false">
      <description>+1 to the combat result of every combat involving at least one friendly Dwarf unit within 12&quot; of the standard.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fd9e-7f8e-9504-c8d9" name="Master Rune of Fear" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit causes fear.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="466c-acb1-b5e8-1bee" name="Master Rune of Grungni" hidden="false">
      <description>Every friendly Dwarf unit within 6&quot; of the standard has a 5+ ward save against shooting attacks and spells defined as magic missiles.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f75c-f1de-423b-472f" name="Strollaz&apos;s Rune" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. After deployment, but before rolling for the first turn, any friendly Dwarf units (not Gyrocopters) within 12&quot; of the standard may make an immediate move, which may be a march but not a charge. These units count as having moved in turn one for shooting.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7c41-739d-93e0-32f6" name="Rune of Slowness" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemies charging the unit subtract D6&quot; from their charge distance; if they fail to reach, the normal failed charge rules apply. With several of these runes, roll a D6 for each and use the highest.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d80a-494e-ab3b-d4f4" name="Rune of Courage" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. The unit is immune to fear and terror.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fcda-35d7-67c4-3fea" name="Rune of Guarding" hidden="false">
      <description>Army Standard Bearer only. Multiples have no further effect. The bearer has a 5+ ward save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e6ee-cbff-77a7-0e1d" name="Rune of Battle" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. The unit adds +1 to its combat result.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2216-6f06-2426-501b" name="Rune of Stoicism" hidden="false">
      <description>Multiples have no further effect. The unit counts as double its actual Unit Strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c195-3f51-4d4e-d1d7" name="Rune of Determination" hidden="false">
      <description>One use only. Multiples have no further effect. The unit may take a Break test on a single D6 instead of 2D6.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="aaad-cc70-d51c-57aa" name="Rune of Sanctuary" hidden="false">
      <description>Each rune gives the unit Magic Resistance (1).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6f92-ccac-a84f-f149" name="Ancestor Rune" hidden="false">
      <description>One use only. When the unit must take a Break test the rune may be expended: on a D6 roll of 4+ the unit, and any character with it, tests as if Stubborn. Only one rune may be expended per Break test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9bd7-b740-aa9e-6500" name="Master Rune of Defence" hidden="false">
      <description>The war machine and its crew always count as in hard cover against enemy shooting.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0820-3c9f-c151-eab7" name="Master Rune of Disguise" hidden="false">
      <description>Until it moves or shoots, the machine cannot be seen, and so cannot be targeted by spells, shot at or charged. Once it has moved or fired, or an enemy unit moves within 3&quot; of it, it is revealed for the rest of the battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4d0c-f001-ade7-e480" name="Master Rune of Immolation" hidden="false">
      <description>One use only. At the end of any round of combat, before the result is worked out, the machine may explode: it and its crew are killed, and each enemy unit in combat with it takes 2D6 magical Strength 4 hits allocated as shooting.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c643-5986-62b2-350a" name="Master Rune of Skewering" hidden="false">
      <description>Bolt Throwers only. One use only. Once per game the Bolt Thrower hits on a 2+ with no modifiers; declare it before rolling to hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5c72-f86f-98c7-6346" name="Rune of Forging" hidden="false">
      <description>Cannons only. Multiples have no further effect. The owning player may re-roll a Misfire on the Artillery dice, to hit or to bounce, but is bound by the second roll.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="043b-619a-7190-960c" name="Rune of Accuracy" hidden="false">
      <description>Grudge Throwers only. Multiples have no further effect. You may re-roll the Scatter dice (not the Artillery dice), but must accept the second roll.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0664-65c9-8a91-870c" name="Rune of Fortune" hidden="false">
      <description>One use only. You may change a dice rolled on the machine&apos;s Misfire chart to a result of 6.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2092-0135-a008-e6a9" name="Rune of Penetrating" hidden="false">
      <description>The Strength of hits from the war machine increases by +1, to a maximum of 10.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d8ec-f632-4fbb-f607" name="Valiant Rune" hidden="false">
      <description>While the war machine is not destroyed, its crew and any Master Engineer who has joined it are Unbreakable.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c7ff-ba6a-3df2-e7cc" name="Stalwart Rune" hidden="false">
      <description>+1 to the crew&apos;s combat result.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2ef4-a9d4-8efb-1773" name="Flakkson&apos;s Rune of Seeking" hidden="false">
      <description>Bolt Throwers only. Each rune gives +1 to hit against targets with the Fly special ability, but the roll needed can never be better than 2+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="606f-047f-2851-cf2b" name="Rune of Reloading" hidden="false">
      <description>The war machine can shoot every turn as long as there is at least one crewman left, even if it rolled a Misfire in the previous turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e738-2b3f-0b04-8741" name="Rune of Burning" hidden="false">
      <description>The war machine makes Flaming attacks.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <catalogueLinks>
    <catalogueLink id="967a-6f7f-5455-31b9" name="Dogs of War" targetId="3604-800a-4012-5da6" type="catalogue" importRootEntries="true"/>
  </catalogueLinks>
</catalogue>